// #taxon[Taxon]
#title[Eulerproduct of Species]

We try to get around the colimit by doing the following construction.
For $p$-local species $A_p$ define the eueler product as the pi-type
$
  prod_(p in PP)^D A_p (n) :-= prod_(p^k||n) A_p (p^k)
$

Does this definition behave well with our dirichlet product?
